# Jaliyah Atkins — Personal Portfolio

A responsive, three-page personal portfolio built with semantic HTML, CSS, and a small amount of JavaScript for accessible form validation.

## Pages and files

- `index.html` — Home page and introduction
- `project.html` — Projects and coursework
- `about.html` — Background, skills, and contact form
- `style.css` — Shared visual design and responsive layouts
- `form.js` — Client-side contact-form validation and accessible feedback

## Design system

The same color palette and typography are used on all three pages:

| Purpose | Color | Hex |
|---|---|---|
| Primary backgrounds and headings | Deep navy | `#102A43` |
| Accent and interactive elements | Dark teal | `#005454` |
| Page background | Warm off-white | `#F7F5F0` |
| Main text | Charcoal | `#243B53` |
| Cards and form surfaces | White | `#FFFFFF` |

The site uses Inter for body text and Montserrat for headings. The layout changes at 768px and 480px so content remains usable on tablets and small screens.

## Accessibility work

Accessibility features included in the project:

- Each page declares its document language, has a descriptive page title and meta description, and uses a single main heading.
- A skip link lets keyboard users bypass repeated navigation.
- Navigation is inside a labeled `nav` landmark; the current page link uses `aria-current="page"`.
- Content uses semantic headings, sections, articles, lists, labels, and form fieldsets.
- Keyboard focus is visible on links, buttons, and form controls.
- The contact form has programmatically associated labels, required fields, helpful descriptions, inline error messages, `aria-invalid` states, and live status feedback.
- Reduced-motion preferences are respected.
- Images are not currently used, so no image alternative text is needed.

### Contrast

The text and control colors were selected to meet WCAG 2.1 AA contrast targets (at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text and meaningful interface components). The core combinations include white on navy, white on dark teal, charcoal on off-white, and dark teal on white. Recheck any future color changes with the [WebAIM Contrast Checker](https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/).

### WAVE testing record

WAVE is an external browser-based checker, so the live published pages must be tested after deployment. The source files have been reviewed for common issues, but a WAVE scan has **not** been run from this local project archive.

